{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc", "file": "references/decision-failure-analysis.md", "content": "# Decision failure analysis: suffix recoloring

In recurring marker/background tasks, demos may support a right-edge recolor while obscuring the qualifying condition. A demo where a row has a very long marker run and only a suffix is recolored does not establish that run length is the criterion; other examples may show suffixes on multiple rows or runs of different lengths. Before applying a memorized threshold or rule, enumerate every candidate row and compare proposed triggers (marker presence, contiguous left-anchored run, majority-of-width, patterns in neighboring rows, or shape alignment) against all demos.

After a wrong submission, treat it as evidence against the entire hypothesis, not simply a nudge to toggle one guessed row. Do not make another output that differs only by a speculative suffix selection. Use an unused demo to target a row pattern on which candidate rules disagree, when its point cost is preferable to further guessing. Remember to maintain the puzzle interface contract: the reply must contain exactly one action JSON on its final line.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1790682233/attempts/90a1f6bd05434476940105e7a5c38287/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzles/continual-arc/references/decision-failure-analysis.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-recovery", "file": "references/task-71ededcc-selective-lines.md", "content": "# Selective 2D gap-completion recurrence: validation caution

The task's demos support a selective rule candidate rather than blanket interpolation. In each orientation independently, lines with an adjacent pair (a contiguous run of ≥2 markers) received color 2 in background positions between marker positions; isolated-only lines were unchanged. The exact interval endpoint rule must be checked carefully: broad fills of all cells between the outermost markers of an eligible line were rejected on a test after several demos. In the test, horizontal row 5 had separate adjacent pairs at columns 6–8 and 10–12 with a gap at column 9; an attempted fill bridged that gap, and row 10 had marker at col 6 separated from pair at cols 12–13; attempted fill bridged the long interval. These exact submissions were rejected, so evidence says at least one such bridge or another selected fill was wrong, not which individual cell.

Do not regard “adjacent pair makes a line eligible” as enough to establish that all intermediate gaps are filled. Candidate distinctions include fill between each contiguous run only, fill gaps between consecutive markers, fill only selected local gaps, or selecting orientation/line based on additional shape context. Compare exact changed cells for every demo (especially demos with multiple runs or separated markers) before applying. With unresolved candidates, spend a demo on an input that has multiple marker runs on a line and isolated marks aligned vertically/horizontally, rather than repeat broad fill guesses.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1790682233/attempts/90a1f6bd05434476940105e7a5c38287/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzles/continual-arc-recovery/references/task-71ededcc-selective-lines.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-recovery", "file": "references/guide-line-rule-transfer-caution.md", "content": "# Guide-line transformation rule transfer caution

A separate task instance showed a full-height color-2 guide at the far-right edge and a nearby color-7 shape on a 0 background. The output added a full-height color-8 stripe at the shape's left edge, parallel to the guide, while shifting the color-7 pattern one column right and preserving the guide. This differs from the known family where a perpendicular color-8 stripe is added without moving the pattern.

Lesson: guide orientation/color and a nearby shape do not uniquely determine the transform. For each task, compare demos cell-by-cell and record (1) stripe orientation, (2) stripe location, (3) whether the pattern is translated or otherwise changed, and (4) what remains fixed. Don't apply a previously seen perpendicular-stripe rule to a superficially similar setup without evidence. See also `arc-reasoning`'s guide-line pitfall; do not assume all guide-line tasks share one rule.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1790682233/attempts/90a1f6bd05434476940105e7a5c38287/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzles/continual-arc-recovery/references/guide-line-rule-transfer-caution.md"}
